      <y>60</y>
      <width>85</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <format>1</format>
      <precision>0</precision>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
      <tooltip>$(P):CH0:MEAN_WIN_10MS (MEAN_WIN_CH0_10MS)

How many of the newest points of $(P):CH0:FBR_RT_10MS_3000DP
that channel's FBR_MEAN_10MS averages. Range 1..1000, default 100;
every channel has its own length.

At 10 ms per point, 100 points is 0.1 s of data and 1000 points is 1 s.
Autosaved, and applied to the very next publication (about 10 Hz).
The record limits the value with DRVL/DRVH and the driver clamps
it again.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
